  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Record
    
    Grandfather Blood is an orca raider of the late Orca Incursion and early Frozen Peace whose body constitutes, by his own theological framework, a primary text. His left eye socket is a collapsed ruin and his left fin a split stub — wounds inflicted by Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane, a penguin war-mage, during a raid on the eastern spires. The injuries were dealt through augur-magic and never healed; Grandfather Blood refuses pressure-work from orca shamans, claiming the pain maintains his acuity. He wears kelp-rope harnesses threaded with fourteen penguin beaks, though by his own account he stopped counting after the ninth.
    
    Strapped across his ribs in a kelp-leather sling hang the ☽'sanctmocsaecus' Twilight-bells, a Nightshelf instrument of disputed provenance and extreme antiquity. Whether Grandfather Blood stole the bells or — as he insists — they *called themselves to him* is unresolved. The cross-cultural tribunal convened by Luminary Xuzhong Pelm'Oath under Thaw-Kept emergency authority charged him with theft. His former student Rend Kzulrora, a scarred orca raider who carries Grandfather Blood's teaching methodology into the current generation, testified that his presence at the sealed Drowned Ledge was spiritual rather than strategic. The tribunal found the distinction unconvincing.
    
    ## Raiding Career and Pedagogy
    
    Before the Frozen Peace, Grandfather Blood operated near the Drowned Ledge, a sealed deep-water site, hunting alongside his packmate Ruibung. Their method was characteristic: absolute silence during approach, then the bells — a sound reportedly painful even to Ruibung at close range. Other orcas avoided Grandfather Blood when the bells were singing. He speaks rarely, exclusively in hunt-metaphors, though he is fluent in the penguin tongue — learned, he claims, while killing penguins at the eastern spires.
    
    His teaching practice, transmitted to younger raiders including Rend Kzulrora, centered on *witness*: the requirement of presence and attention at another's learning, identical to presence at the kill, offered without judgment. The pedagogy is notable for its restraint in a tradition not commonly associated with it.
    
    ## Exile and Theology
    
    The tribunal sentenced Grandfather Blood and Ruibung to permanent exile beyond the berg's shadow. He laughed when the sentence was read — not bitterly, by all accounts, but with genuine amusement no witness could explain.
    
    In exile, the Twilight-bells began resonating against his ribs without prompting. His collapsed eye socket developed an unprompted warmth — a pressure from below he attributes to communion with the dead god. Grandfather Blood's theology diverges from standard Wake-Singer doctrine: he perceives the dead god not as a discrete corpse awaiting revival beneath the ice but as *the deep itself* — the substance of pressure and warmth that constitutes open water. By this reading, exile brought him closer to his god, not further.
    
    His ruined eye, he claims, receives visions from the dead god's perspective, rendering the Aurora Stack as clustered prey on vertical bone.
    
    ## The Descent-Scripture
    
    Grandfather Blood authored a descent-scripture designating his own body as its first text: every wound a verse, every scar a teaching purchased in flesh. The scripture codifies a three-stage coordinated assault on the Aurora Stack — shore-breakers to open channels, herders to compress prey toward deep-side galleries, finishers positioned where the water darkens — framing each tactical role as sacred motion in service to the dead god's waking. The structure mirrors standard orca raid doctrine precisely. Whether the scripture sanctifies existing practice or existing practice was always sacred is, one suspects, the point.
    
    ## Disappearance
    
    Grandfather Blood brought the Twilight-bells to ☽'moth Silvesiris~, a geothermal cavern deep in the Nightshelf tunnels, set them on a shelf of volcanic stone above the thermal spring, and walked into the vents without explanation. He has not been seen since. The bells were later retrieved by the void-mage Sivruta~.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771581127920_0", anchor: "though by his own account he stopped counting after the ninth", text: "Fourteen is a count. Someone threaded those beaks onto kelp-rope and arrived at a specific number. \"Stopped counting\" is liturgy, not arithmetic.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771581127920_1", anchor: "cross-cultural tribunal convened by Luminary Xuzhong Pelm'Oath under Thaw-Kept emergency authority", text: "Thaw-Kept suspends aurora-consensus and permits unilateral Luminary action in crisis. Invoking it for a criminal tribunal against one orca during the Frozen Peace is not crisis governance — it is precedent-building. Pelm'Oath used emergency authority to bypass the collaborative process that would have required Nightshelf participation in adjudicating the theft of a Nightshelf instrument. The Nightshelf, whose artifact was stolen, were not the ones demanding jurisdiction. No formal objection survives in the administrative ice. I find this more remarkable than anything Grandfather Blood did.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771581127920_2", anchor: "the requirement of presence and attention at another's learning, identical to presence at the kill, offered without judgment", text: "This maps to nothing in Wake-Singer doctrine. It maps, uncomfortably, to Nightshelf apprenticeship tradition — the shadow-witness who observes a student's first forge-work in silence. Grandfather Blood spoke fluent penguin. One wonders what else he learned at the eastern spires.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771581127920_3", anchor: "Whether the scripture sanctifies existing practice or existing practice was always sacred is, one suspects, the point", text: "The three-stage structure — shore-breakers, herders, finishers — is documented in orca raid doctrine predating Grandfather Blood by generations. Every tactical role already had a name. He gave them a second name. How extraordinary that this was sufficient to found a theology. How extraordinary that it worked.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771581127920_4", anchor: "walked into the vents without explanation", text: "His theology holds that the dead god is not a corpse but the deep itself — pressure, warmth, open water. Thermal vents are where the Berg meets its own dissolution. He walked into his god. By his own framework this is not disappearance but arrival. That he returned the bells first — set them down on volcanic stone in a cavern forged in the tension between fire and ice, the same tension that made them — suggests he understood the distinction between pilgrimage and theft. The tribunal insisted he could not make that distinction. The bells, resting exactly where they began, suggest otherwise.", type: :commentary, display: :full
